  "question": {
    "html": "<p>Containers A and B contain the same substance at the same temperature. In container A the substance is in the gas state. In container B the substance is in the liquid state. The average kinetic energy of the molecules in container A is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"E_{A}\"></span> and the average kinetic energy of the molecules in container B is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"E_{B}\"></span>. What is true about <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"E_{A}\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"E_{B}\"></span>?   </p>\n<p></p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\">\n<li data-label=\"A\">Based on the information provided, the relationship between <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"E_{A}\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"E_{B}\"></span> cannot be determined.</li>\n<li data-label=\"B\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"E_{A}&gt;E_{B}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"C\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"E_{A}&lt;E_{B}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"D\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"E_{A}=E_{B}\"></span></li>\n</ol>"
  },
